ertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;moved to terminate his contract, which ran to 2027, after a thigh injury in training on 11 August; he made six appearances last season. A financial settlement is still being negotiated and is expected to be resolved by 1 September.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Chelsea are locking down the academy.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Shumaira Mheuka</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, the 18-year-old Premier League 2 player of the season, is to sign a long-term deal to 2033 before going out on loan; the club has also handed professional or improved terms to eight further academy players.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Charlotte FC lost two players to surgery on 6 August.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Nimfasha Berchimas</span><span>&nbsp;is out roughly twelve weeks with a broken foot and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Aron John</span><span style="color:#000000;font-wei